            <ArticleTitle>CT imaging features of carotidynia: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>84-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1552-6569.2007.00232.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite denial as a disease entity, carotidynia had shown relatively concordant imaging finding as an inflammatory process surrounding the carotid bifurcation area. We report serial computed tomography (CT) images of a case with carotidynia that showed the layered thickening of the carotid wall with self-limiting disease course.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
